    "result_text": "The full build passes. Let me summarize the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `GOLD` membership tier rule: an owner's tier becomes `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the codebase's established pattern (a snapshot count recorded at create time and read by the mapper, exactly like `namesakeCount`), I kept each concern in its own small unit:\n\n1. **`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`** (new function class) \u2014 a single-responsibility pipeline step mirroring `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`. It runs right after `AssignOwnerHousehold` (once the shared `householdId` is assigned) and before save, counting existing owners with the same `householdId` plus this owner, giving the household size *after this create*. Standalone owners (no `householdId`) get size 1.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in between `assignHousehold` and `assignBulkSignupWarning`, with the same `transaction` governance as its neighbours.\n\n3. **`Owner`** \u2014 added the persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter, so the value survives to the later `GET /api/owners/{id}` read.\n\n4. **Schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier`** \u2014 added the GOLD branch (household size \u2265 3) ahead of the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic, keeping the tier decision in the one place that already owns it. Also added `householdSize` to the `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignore list for consistency.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold`) and the full suite pass: `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
